<description>&lt;p&gt;Mali forces have retaken Kidal as jihadist attacks intensify, and a Mali drone strike killed 13 civilians while claiming to target militants. In Niger, a convoy carrying Governor Bago collided with a car, killing four students, a driver and a young woman, and Niger accused Chad of a drone attack that killed two civilians. Algeria has deployed troops to Niger to protect energy assets, its first foreign mission in over 50 years. Militants now control at least 40% of Burkina Faso, a critic of Mali’s junta was forcibly disappeared, and the junta stripped five more exiled critics of nationality. The conflict produced 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipwFBVV95cUxPWVZQcnVSbVZlRVVUOGd4OUdINXVJc0NPMlhwTnc3d2N1RHNNOElYb3ZjVXBWOUp0Z1I3a292M0pkVW00VWliTi1YelNmRlMtSU1vM29qVEFQek1acWxDMk1lMVRUUzBNUzhRN3BlUlY2SkRWZHA0RFBqTmtSdy1CZ05KT1Q0M1pZMW1QVTlVN0FEREhJa3g0TFphSFZuX1Jud0F1eWxkMA?oc=5&quot;&gt;AP News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;ACI Africa&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilwFBVV95cUxNaWxKVWFjS0cyVWZ2dnUwV2JPdS1DSHEtaUVfNVBoWGFpZFNYRU5fTGFOQW5QaktvZkFxdFhMeVJwejJ2MXZ5TVNwY0ZYXzlGdGh2SFlWUHM4WHRDT1p4TmNCb3BiQTRGaWpBdk8ySFY3NE9HVkp0MVNaTzc4SnFYaDI1YTR6Rkh5MzFjN0plR1NGSUhMcWFJ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Human Rights Watch&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Modern Ghana&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cUxPTGNfVzhZTy04YmZuc2IzM0hIdDVHWjhWUUZ5LUZ6SHMwdG81TlVoXzhlellXZFo3TUVtcncyanlhQzRPaGZ0ZHRwVHUzOVJUNEpfZUNzVk1ZRHduZHZDMXZpQWNEOHBFdDR6d3VxcG1ZQ1lvUEVhWEpPU2tCWGlJdUY2cVpPM2djSkRONHBjRUZpenpIMDRTWDVCSkZKUQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Genocide Watch&lt;/a&gt;,